{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011164-healing-magic","id":1011164,"title":"Healing Magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-02T12:13:52-08:00","id":1011164,"title":"Healing Magic","content":"I'm pretty excited that I'm caught up on reading the forums, finally. I read 22 months of posts over the last 6 weeks.<br /> <br /> I'm getting ready to run my 2e game. My original 1e game AP can be found here: <a href=\"http://mage-doomcrew.obsidianportal.com/posts?order_by=oldest&amp;page=1\" target=\"_blank\">http://mage-doomcrew.obsidianportal....=oldest&amp;page=1</a><br /> <br /> Am I right that the following is a legal ritual spell:<br /> <br /> Mage: Life 5, Gnosis 3, Body Control Rote w/Order Specialty at max skill<br /> <br /> Reach: Heal Lethal + 2 Reach, Advanced Duration + 1 Reach, so no Paradox<br /> <br /> Yantras: + 2 Runes, + 3 Persona, + 6 Rote Mudra <br /> <br /> Penalty: 65,536 x Healing Rate - 22, One Day -2<br /> <br /> Dice Pool = Life 5 + Gnosis 3 + Ritual 5 (5 hours) + Persona 3 + Demesne 2 + Mudras 6 - Potency 22 (16) - One Day 2 + Willpower 3 = 3 dice<br /> <br /> This ritual would allow a Mage to heal 1 Lethal per turn for a day.<br /> <br /> Also, is there an easier way to do this?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 12-02-2016, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T13:03:26-08:00","id":1011178,"title":"","content":"Life 5 and Gnosis 3? What is this monstrosity? But to the point... You would heal 22(potency) lethal damage every Gnosis interval which at this level is 1 hour.<br /> <br /> Edit: Yup. My bad. I thought that you are talking about Knit. I don't know why.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 12-03-2016, 05:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T14:04:09-08:00","id":1011212,"title":"","content":"You need at least Gnosis 5 to have an Arcanum at 5 dots in 2E, but the basic idea is sound.<br /> <br /> Everyone always seems to latch onto the fast-healing aspect of Body Control when they pick up the book, but there are so many easier ways to heal yourself unless you're expecting to continuously get stabbed for a few hours straight. Just cast Knit when you get hurt, or do Pattern Restoration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T19:32:19-08:00","id":1011314,"title":"","content":"Well the advantage of using BC is that it is continuous regeneration without any further casting needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 12-03-2016, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T20:30:12-08:00","id":1011332,"title":"","content":"Mudra bonus caps at +5 post-errata and Body Control's primary factor is Duration. Getting that free Potency is going to cost you another Reach.<br /> <br /> Also (Holy undeclared story elements, Batman!) what on Earth are those Demesne and Persona boosts actually representative of?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T21:07:03-08:00","id":1011357,"title":"","content":"Slightly condensed version of the OP: with Potency 16 (or 15 if you round time increments down as the spell does in its example text), Body Control can heal 1 lethal damage every turn. You'll also have +16 Initiative and a variety of narrative health benefits that we don't care about. There are a few ways to get the dicepool for Potency that high, but the core idea does what you want it to do, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 12-03-2016, 12:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-02T22:41:55-08:00","id":1011378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011164-healing-magic?p=1011332#post1011332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mudra bonus caps at +5 post-errata and Body Control's primary factor is Duration. Getting that free Potency is going to cost you another Reach.<br /> <br /> Also (Holy undeclared story elements, Batman!) what on Earth are those Demesne and Persona boosts actually representative of?</div> </div> </div> </div>Tai-Chi Student (Persona) doing exercise in a <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">kwoon (Demesne).</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T00:00:05-08:00","id":1011393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011164-healing-magic?p=1011212#post1011212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You need at least Gnosis 5 to have an Arcanum at 5 dots in 2E, but the basic idea is sound.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not true actually! As per the Experiences table on page 83, it's just one Experience more expensive to go above your Gnosis-derived limit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12714-aranaira","name":"AranaiRa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12714_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T00:11:55-08:00","id":1011397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AranaiRa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011164-healing-magic?p=1011393#post1011393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not true actually! As per the Experiences table on page 83, it's just one Experience more expensive to go above your Gnosis-derived limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is true. Page 86:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gnosis limits the upper limit of a mage\u2019s Arcana. A mage\u2019s<br /> highest Arcanum can be three dots at Gnosis 1, four dots at<br /> Gnosis 3, and five dots at Gnosis 5. That mage\u2019s other Arcana<br /> are limited to a maximum of two dots at Gnosis 1, three dots<br /> at Gnosis 2, four dots at Gnosis 4, and five dots at Gnosis 6. </div> </div> </div>EDIT: These limits can also be seen in the Gnosis table on page 86.<br /> <br /> The character advancement table is referring to a mage's <i>Path-derived</i> limits on untrained Arcanum learning, as explained on page 84:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Limits of Arcana<br /> Each Path provides two Ruling Arcana, one Inferior Arcanum,<br /> and seven Common Arcana. The difference determines the cost<br /> of buying dots in the Arcanum, and at what point a character<br /> requires a teacher.<br /> <br /> Arcanum Maximum Untrained<br /> Ruling 5 dots<br /> Common 4 dots<br /> Inferior 2 dots<br /> <br /> Characters can buy up to the above limits for four Experiences<br /> per dot, which can be regular or Arcane Experiences. Exceeding<br /> the limit increases the cost to five Experiences, requires a teacher<br /> who already knows the dot-level sought, and can only be bought<br /> with regular Experiences. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus","name":"General Tacticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T01:06:32-08:00","id":1011405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>General Tacticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011164-healing-magic?p=1011397#post1011397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is true. -snip-<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Welp, made a fool out of myself. Thanks for correcting me though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12714-aranaira","name":"AranaiRa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12714_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T01:16:35-08:00","id":1011406,"title":"","content":"No worries! It's confusingly laid out, for sure, to have two different limits on Arcanum dots, based on different criteria, one of which can be exceeded and one of which cannot. I didn't think it was true either until I looked it up in response to Caladriu's post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12425-general-tacticus","name":"General Tacticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T01:22:38-08:00","id":1011408,"title":"","content":"I think I asked for this to be clarified in the errata thread, yeah. It's confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T10:50:28-08:00","id":1011572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011164-healing-magic?p=1011332#post1011332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mudra bonus caps at +5 post-errata and Body Control's primary factor is Duration. Getting that free Potency is going to cost you another Reach.<br /> <br /> Also (Holy undeclared story elements, Batman!) what on Earth are those Demesne and Persona boosts actually representative of?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well this is a similar spell called Control of Body with potency as primary. Also, the book says Mudras are capped at 5 before the order specialty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 12-03-2016, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T11:06:59-08:00","id":1011583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011164-healing-magic?p=1011572#post1011572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well this is a similar spell called Control of Body with potency as primary. Also, the book says Mudras are capped at 5 before the order specialty.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Step Five: Primary Factor<br /> Determine which Factor is the Primary Factor. This is either<br /> Potency or Duration, with the rule of thumb of \u201cwhichever<br /> Factor you immediately think of when you think of a more<br /> powerful version of the spell.\u201d <b>The Primary Factor of a given<br /> spell effect is always the same; you can\u2019t make a creative thaumaturgy<br /> spell that\u2019s identical to another spell except with a<br /> different Primary Factor.</b> </div> </div> </div>Mage 2e, p. 127.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T11:35:19-08:00","id":1011593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011164-healing-magic?p=1011583#post1011583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Mage 2e, p. 127.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's not the same spell. Mine just has the regeneration. <br /> <br /> PS: That's the silliest new rule in the whole system. It runs completely counter to the idea of improvised magic.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T11:45:39-08:00","id":1011598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1011164-healing-magic?p=1011593#post1011593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's not the same spell. Mine just has the regeneration.<br /> <br /> PS: That's the silliest new rule in the whole system. It runs completely counter to the idea of improvised magic.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Without the rule, spells would not have a set and expected Primary Factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T13:34:30-08:00","id":1011638,"title":"","content":"To answer the OP: It depends on on your interpretation of the rules. If you want to run entirely RAW, then yes, you could amplify Body Control until you're healing a lethal level a turn. If you want to dig into the spell a little, it ostensibly works by giving you control over natural bodily functions and to direct them more efficiently, which places a natural limit on the spell.<br /> <br /> Personally, I've allowed a spell like this in my game. It's actually not <i>as</i> useful as you might expect in combat but it can definitely turn the tide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T01:37:16-08:00","id":1012447,"title":"","content":"Giving yourself armor with &quot;Transform Life&quot; would e.g. usually be much more useful and a lot simpler. But if you really want a healing over time spell that badly: go for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T03:25:18-08:00","id":1012473,"title":"","content":"I've houseruled Body Control (and other &quot;regeneration&quot; powers) not to shorten the healing interval, but to add Potency to damage healed naturally (so, 1+Potency Bashing every 15 mins; 1+Potency Lethal every 48 hours), for sanity's sake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T08:01:08-08:00","id":1012581,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the suggestions, everyone. I was just curious about the legality under RAW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}